achievement_examples_61389930		Next, a progress achievement. This one needs [progress_achievement.stat_max] steps to complete. You have [progress_achievement.stat_progress] steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	277	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_b42a4323		Added 1 step. You now have [progress_achievement.stat_progress] steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	282	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_11bc50e0		Added 4 steps. You now have [progress_achievement.stat_progress] steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	286	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_19fe54cb		Set progress to 5. You now have [progress_achievement.stat_progress] steps completed. Note that you can't reverse progress - if your progress is higher than 5, it won't be reduced to 5.	game/achievements.rpy	290	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_633580b3		Reset progress. You now have [progress_achievement.stat_progress] steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	294	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_a988c050		Note that the progress you add is {i}not{/i} rollback or repeat-safe! If you roll back, you can add more progress. You will also add more progress picking the same option multiple times.	game/achievements.rpy	298	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_7afdfc90		We can fix that with the next type of progress progression: using sets.	game/achievements.rpy	299	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_2dfde24f		This achievement uses a set to track unique progress towards the achievement.	game/achievements.rpy	300	"[what]"
achievement_example_add_progress_bfcc7dba		You don't have to do anything special to use it; just set a stat_max and use the add_set_progress method.	game/achievements.rpy	301	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_df857bfe		You saw the good end! You now have [set_progress_achievement.stat_progress] unique steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	306	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_1d8592eb		You saw the bad end! You now have [set_progress_achievement.stat_progress] unique steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	310	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_3966b5e8		You saw the neutral end! You now have [set_progress_achievement.stat_progress] unique steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	314	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_029f8d42		You saw the second bad end! You now have [set_progress_achievement.stat_progress] unique steps completed.	game/achievements.rpy	318	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_a0a97bcf		This set progress {i}is{/i} rollback safe. If you roll back or choose the same ending over and over, it will not count towards the achievement's completion multiple times.	game/achievements.rpy	324	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_c7039a8a		Note also that there are 4 possible values that can be added to the set, but the achievement only requires 3 of them to be added to unlock.	game/achievements.rpy	325	"[what]"
achievement_example_set_progress_238d4031		The rest of the achievements are fairly straightforward to achieve.	game/achievements.rpy	326	"[what]"
