farmers_market_577cf6ce		As you approach the town's central plaza your ears prick up at the hum of generators and the murmur of a small crowd.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	19	"[what]"
farmers_market_0ed4565c		Your foxen senses catch the scent of baked goods, hot cider, and herbs on the light breeze that carries away the last bit of the summer day's humidity.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	21	"[what]"
farmers_market_8f8ecf1d		The farmers market is in full swing for harvest season.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	23	"[what]"
farmers_market_b7c3d608		Orchard vendors sell more of the early season peaches; other stalls sell the last of the season's blackberries. The usual veggie stands have a bounty of fresh treasures--corn, broccoli, peppers, radishes.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	25	"[what]"
farmers_market_09757ae8		A beekeeper has paired up with a woodworker to selling wooden wands and bread bowls alongside clover and wildflower honeys.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	27	"[what]"
farmers_market_2e947bfa		Rows of tents offer unique, handcrafted goods from merchants in the surrounding regions who've come to this town to peddle their wares.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	29	"[what]"
farmers_market_5127f113		There's even another fox spirit selling lucky talismans. The talismans are real magic, though the workings are quite small; it's better not to swing the karmic balance too far in any direction unless you really know what you're doing.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	31	"[what]"
farmers_market_61507c60		The first farmers market of the season is always a big one. You love to see the same faces year after year. It's a good time to meet new merchants, too.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	33	"[what]"
farmers_market_88eed8c1		You pick up some veggies, a cup of black coffee, and buy a loaf of bread from a baker who drove 3 hours to be here. It's divine.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	35	"[what]"
farmers_market_7ddc8360		Your bags are much heavier after a good lap around the produce side of the market. You head to a flower stand you've bought from in the past in search of your usual marigold and sunflowers. Your favorites.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	37	"[what]"
farmers_market_bcf50d7e		You hear her voice before you see her.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	41	"[what]"
farmers_market_f6486ad1	e	"Coming right up! Let me get those bagged for you."	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	43	e happy "[what]"
farmers_market_663cd7c7		A customer hands Erin a bouquet of daisies and she turns around to place it in a water-sealed paper bag.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	45	"[what]"
farmers_market_ce909cc2		She's smiling when she returns the bouquet to the customer, then sees you and waves.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	47	"[what]"
farmers_market_9133cd96	e	"Aya! Are you here to get flowers??"	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	49	e excited "[what]"
farmers_market_e8ee232d	a	"I sure am. I didn't expect to see you here!"	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	51	a happy "[what]"
farmers_market_dce5db5f	e	"It's a part time gig! I helped unload everything. I could probably give you some ideas on what looked the prettiest today! What would you think about this little bouquet of lavender and larkspur?"	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	53	e happy "[what]"
farmers_market_marigold_7e9996c8	a	"Thanks, but I think I'll get my usual. A bouquet each of marigold and sunflowers, please."	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	78	a "[what]"
farmers_market_marigold_af5cbc90	e	"Oooh how pretty! I love that, I'll bag those for you."	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	80	e "[what]"
farmers_market_lavender_7efa1c85	a	"That's a good suggestion, I'll take the lavender and larkspur."	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	86	a "[what]"
farmers_market_lavender_718c390f		She beams at you and nearly bounces to fetch a bouquet of purple and blue sprigs.	game/script files/3_farmersmarket.rpy	88	"[what]"
