rain_wake_early_3e69546a		Erin is curled up at near your back with the blankets piled atop her. One arm escaped the blanket nest and flopped to the side. She's not touching you, but... Your fluffy tail is once again draped across her body.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	362	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_e8d47036		Weak morning sunlight peeks through the shut curtains, casting cool rays across her bundled-up form.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	364	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_1e3d75fe		You roll over carefully. When you slip your tail gently off her she mumbles a bit in protest.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	366	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_036881c7		She's {i}so{/i} cute sleepy.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	368	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_07cead05	a	(I wonder what it would be like to wake up like this every morning?)	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	370	a happy "[what]"
rain_wake_early_29948fad		You're sure you can't be thinking like that.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	372	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_37d8e076	a	"I have to stop!"	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	374	a neutral "[what]"
rain_wake_early_270d4868		You clap a hand over your mouth in horror.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	376	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_4a62bc54	a	(I did NOT mean to say that out loud.)	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	378	a "[what]"
rain_wake_early_920cc6f4		But you didn't seem to wake her, thankfully.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	380	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_8bda6c29		You slip out of the bed and tiptoe to the bathroom to get yourself ready for the day.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	382	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_494e569e		You take your time. When you're feeling fresh and ready for the day you plod over to the kitchen. Your ankle feels better today.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	384	"[what]"
rain_wake_early_75dec8ed	a	"Maybe I should make her breakfast."	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	385	a happy "[what]"
rain_sleep_in_e3dca6fd		The bed is empty when you wake, Erin's blankets folded neatly on the side table.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	394	"[what]"
rain_sleep_in_87d06292		You rub the sleep from your eyes and slip from the bed, heading to the bathroom.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	396	"[what]"
rain_sleep_in_bb24c7d9	a	(Did she leave?)	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	398	a neutral "[what]"
rain_sleep_in_c814a3f1		You get ready for the day and plod to the kitchen. Your ankle feels better today.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	400	"[what]"
rain_sleep_in_83ecffa5		Something's out of place.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	404	"[what]"
rain_sleep_in_a9dfb732		There's a plate on the dining table with an overturned bowl on it. You lift the bowl, revealing still-warm eggs and a bagel inside.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	406	"[what]"
rain_sleep_in_67f92117		It looks like Erin cooked breakfast! You need a drink, then you should find her and thank her.	game/script files/5_rain.rpy	408	"[what]"
the_call_79ec2e2d		You're filling a glass of water when you hear Erin's muffled voice. She must be out on the balcony, and by the sound of it she's not having a very fun conversation.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	6	"[what]"
the_call_4f192de4		When she comes in she seems deflated.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	9	"[what]"
the_call_8568a042	a	"Oh, there you are! Were you on the phone?"	game/script files/6_call.rpy	11	a neutral "[what]"
the_call_cc32c9bb	e	"Yeah. It was my parents. They want me to come back to the city."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	13	e neutral "[what]"
the_call_acdba22b		Your stomach drops. This can't be happening.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	15	"[what]"
the_call_64bceb82	a	"I see. So... are you going?"	game/script files/6_call.rpy	17	a "[what]"
the_call_a3dccbdb	e	"Sigh. I haven't decided yet, to be honest. It's nice out here, and..."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	19	e gloom "[what]"
the_call_90956e26		She looks sidelong at you through lowered lashes.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	21	"[what]"
the_call_b626b1b4	e	"I've found somewhere I like being. This feels like a place I could belong."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	23	e happy "[what]"
the_call_94004a03		Oh.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	25	"[what]"
the_call_a92bf360	a	"Don't you want to finish college?"	game/script files/6_call.rpy	27	a "[what]"
the_call_88655d79	e	"There are other ways. I could postpone it or do it online. Anyway, the point is that I'm not really ready to go back to the city. I don't want to go."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	29	e neutral "[what]"
the_call_6b175d5a	a	"What about your parents?"	game/script files/6_call.rpy	31	a "[what]"
the_call_3301b220	e	"What about them? I appreciate that they want to look out for me, but I'm doing just fine. I'm not doing anything wrong by trying to be happy."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	33	e "[what]"
the_call_95929a0a	a	"That's kind of a great outlook."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	35	a happy "[what]"
the_call_c56df087	e	"Right?"	game/script files/6_call.rpy	37	e happy "[what]"
the_call_21bfed73		You can't help yourself. You reach out and rub her shoulder.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	39	"[what]"
the_call_8d866e8e	a	"I'm glad you found somewhere you want to be. Belonging somewhere is something everyone needs, humans and spirits alike."	game/script files/6_call.rpy	41	a "[what]"
the_call_30479eef		She smiles shyly at you.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	43	"[what]"
the_call_489753aa		That's when YOU get a call. One you're totally unprepared for.	game/script files/6_call.rpy	45	"[what]"
the_plan_11bf6f3f	a	"What do you mean they want us to close the bookstore?!"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	9	a shocked "[what]"
the_plan_8a48d829		Erin's eyes go wide and she looks horrified.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	11	"[what]"
the_plan_532121f5	a	"I told you, I'm not closing it! I'll figure something out. Tell them I said that."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	13	a "[what]"
the_plan_7b63d0f0		You end the call and shove your phone into the pocket of your sweatpants.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	15	"[what]"
the_plan_88154d28	e	"Why would the store close? Doesn't your family own it?"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	17	e shocked "[what]"
the_plan_e88269f6	a	"We do own it, but there was a problem with a malicious spirit about half a century ago. My parents made a deal with a more powerful entity to ward the store, but it seems like they neglected to pay it back in full."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	19	a sad "[what]"
the_plan_f7340cc6	e	"What's left to pay?"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	21	e neutral "[what]"
the_plan_a1da0204	a	"One hundred. Due before the new year."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	23	a gloom "[what]"
the_plan_3ca01438	e	"That's a problem because...?"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	25	e "[what]"
the_plan_238ec889	a	"One hundred thousand. We'll be cutting it close."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	27	a "[what]"
the_plan_0fdfd9e3		It's a daunting number for a little bookshop but she's nonplussed.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	30	"[what]"
the_plan_d9bde5f5	e	"I could help you!"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	32	e happy "[what]"
the_plan_abfb917a	a	"How?"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	34	a neutral "[what]"
the_plan_b1ff9e09	e	"My major is marketing! I can come up with a plan that'll bring in more business. We could even find some sponsors who want to invest in the bookstore and would cover that cost, easy."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	36	e excited "[what]"
the_plan_1a88e713	a	"I had no idea you had that skillset! Will people really just... give us money?"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	38	a "[what]"
the_plan_4349ef59		Your brow furrows.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	40	"[what]"
the_plan_147ef0b8		Erin frowns a little and reaches up to smooth the wrinkle with a gentle thumb.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	42	"[what]"
the_plan_a84bf69d	e	"Don't worry. We'll get you sorted, no problem."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	44	e "[what]"
the_plan_1f49b9d4		You spend the rest of the afternoon drawing up a plan.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	46	"[what]"
plan_execution_dd84f44e		Erin finishes jotting down notes in the composition notepad you grabbed from a bookshelf.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	55	"[what]"
plan_execution_d1e4cf72	e	"And that's how we'll do it."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	57	e happy "[what]"
plan_execution_01a54ead	a	"I'm willing to give it a try. Thank you for doing this, Erin."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	59	a neutral "[what]"
plan_execution_bbc610be	e	"It's no problem! Like I said, this is my thing."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	61	e "[what]"
plan_execution_09c13d51	e	"Anyway... I should probably get going. Gotta get a change of clothes for my shift at the cornerstore later."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	63	e neutral "[what]"
plan_execution_482f6dda	a	"Yeah. Before you go, I just wanted to apologize for how I acted back... before the rain. That wasn't fair, and you were right."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	65	a sad "[what]"
plan_execution_ed5557f2		She smiles a little.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	67	"[what]"
plan_execution_6ff7ae36	a	"And... thank you again for bringing me home safe and sound."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	69	a neutral "[what]"
plan_execution_8523c6af	e	"Apology accepted. I'd come to your rescue anytime."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	71	e happy "[what]"
plan_execution_d548170a		When you walk her downstairs to the front door and open it a gust of chilly autumn air leaves you shivering.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	73	"[what]"
plan_execution_eaa247f8	a	"Wait, let me get you something before you leave."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	75	a happy "[what]"
plan_execution_638c6f32	e	"Sure!"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	77	e "[what]"
plan_execution_d0d732aa		You return with one of your light jackets in tow.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	79	"[what]"
plan_execution_f3faace1	a	"Um, you can borrow this. Don't catch a cold."	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	81	a tsuntsun "[what]"
plan_execution_4172ad89	e	"Oh Aya, thank you. You ARE sweet!"	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	83	e blush "[what]"
plan_execution_2804b508		You wave a hand at her to brush off the praise.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	85	"[what]"
plan_execution_d9a747ab		She starts down the road, spinning around at the corner to wave at you one more time.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	87	"[what]"
plan_execution_478e5f72		She said she likes being here, and she's quickly entwining herself in different parts of your life.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	89	"[what]"
plan_execution_1d3c0eae		Maybe she WILL stay.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	91	"[what]"
plan_execution_4c56d31f		Opening your heart still feels risky, but maybe Erin is worth the risk.	game/script files/7_plan.rpy	93	"[what]"
lost_market_0c24f3a2		The next couple of weeks are peaceful. The air keeps getting cooler, the farmers markets have been lovely.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	5	"[what]"
lost_market_67322d3f		You get into a sort of routine with Erin.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	7	"[what]"
lost_market_bookstore_42aafc57		The bookstore is the perfect environment to meet up and talk about marketing plans, surrounded by generations of words of wisdom and creative ideas.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	23	"[what]"
lost_market_office_c0fadb38		The office has lots of room to meet with people and map out plans on the big glass tables.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	30	"[what]"
lost_market_aya_house_fb4dbac7		Your house. It's comfortable, private, and you can make as much of a mess of notes and projects as you want.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	37	"[what]"
lost_market_cont_a36a383a		When Erin isn't working, you make drafts, print posters and fliers, and otherwise enact the Great Bookstore Revival.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	44	"[what]"
lost_market_cont_e0f771a6		Erin calls investors and organizations who might help with such a funding project while you call local shops to discuss business collaborations.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	46	"[what]"
lost_market_cont_61a940f4		She's so supportive and optimistic that you can't help but catch her energy and feel that way, too.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	48	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_b7dd6aa6		Erin didn't show up at the usual meeting time.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	61	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_f6e9b210		You wait twenty minutes.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	63	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_99611a9f		Twenty minutes turns into an hour, then two. She's not answering her phone.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	67	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_c54d5a4b		You check near the bookstore. She's not there.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	69	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_3668fd93		You call the cornerstore and the orchard office and are told she's not there either.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	73	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_6ad54c59		You bite your lip. What if something's happened	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	77	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_a17cdba9		At home, you put on a jacket and sneakers and pace in the front room, trying to decide where to start looking for her.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	80	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_4d91b390		There's a knock at the door, and you run to open it.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	86	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_b29c186f	a	"Erin--! Oh, Lydia? What are you doing here?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	88	a shocked "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_b36daeab		It's not who you were hoping it would be, and judging by Lydia's expression, you're not about to be happy that she's here either.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	93	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_7c693198	lyd	"You haven't found a spell to fix that lamp yet, right?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	95	lyd "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_606730db	a	"N-no, not yet, we're planning to go find the Lost Market in a few days. Do you want to come in?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	97	a neutral "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_a6fc6eee	lyd	"The Market came early, Aya."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	99	lyd "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_02b18df7		No... Oh no...	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	101	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_0d2ac1be	a	"She couldn't have..."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	103	a shocked "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_2214fcf2	lyd	"She did. Terry the fox spirit saw her go in unaccompanied and ran to tell me."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	105	lyd "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_88ebf329	a	"Shit. And you didn't call..."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	107	a "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_216ff4b0	lyd	"...because I still don't own a phone."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	109	lyd "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_d9352fa7		Of course this ancient cat still hasn't gotten a phone.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	111	"[what]"
lost_market_find_out_cbe839f0	a	"I need to find her, fast. Where's the entrance?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	113	a neutral "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_fe65986a	lyd	"The alley between the grocer and the barber. Be safe, and be quick. I really do hope you find her in time."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	115	lyd "[what]"
lost_market_find_out_25f48d46		You run.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	120	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_bed32f5c		You run faster than you ever have before. Your legs and lungs burn and you gasp for air, but push through the exhaustion and make it to the entrance.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	134	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_8f2d0f46		No matter where it shows up, the entrance to the Lost Market always looks like a really, REALLY long and dark alleyway with floating lights flickering at the far end of it.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	136	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_00212734		It doesn't usually pose a risk to humans, since you have to be a spirit or in a pact with a spirit to be able to see it at all.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	138	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_40eeef0b		And if you can't see it, it can't see you back.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	140	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_27dfb119		You slow down and start walking down the alley. It's faster to walk than to run. It's tricky like that.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	145	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_4821b237		The floating lights start to illuminate faint edges of structures in the alleyway; the ground, the brick walls, loose rocks, some cardboard boxes.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	147	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_920b1556		The amber glow grows. You step out of the alley into a street full of spirits of all shape and size.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	149	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_41211a74		As naturally as breathing, you shift fully into your spirit form: an enormous pink three-tailed fox with small red horns. You sniff the air and stretch out each leg, feeling your paws against the cool ground.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	174	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_9876b464		Tall, shapeless giants and tiny floating imps float alongside animal spirits like yourself.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	178	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_7f8b2529		You don't waste any time.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	180	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_b3d61eec		You run, weaving through the silent crowd, following the faint, unmistakable glowing red tether of the pact you made. Your sensitive nose picks up the citrus and apple scent of Erin's shampoo.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	182	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_c6e947ac		You have to go faster!	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	184	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_5f8ab956		You run and run, and finally you know you're drawing near when the tether glows brighter.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	186	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_348242b1		A small crowd has formed a circle around Erin, and she's not alone.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	188	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_487f6ade		She's standing boldly before an oni girl with impossibly sharp horns. A red ribbon--not yours--floats around the oni, and a tendril of it begins to reach towards Erin.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	210	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_f9bed2ef		You leap, snapping at the ribbon. It shatters into sparkling shards of light between your sharp teeth.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	212	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_901981c2	"Oni"	"You dare to intefere? This human wished to make a pact with me, fox. I was simply going to lead her out of here."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	217	"Oni" "[what]"
lost_market_inside_2a7d49cf	a	"In exchange for what?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	220	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_25b5e034	"Oni"	"A trifling matter. She was to bring me across to the mortal realm with her."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	224	"Oni" "[what]"
lost_market_inside_0025e6f6	a	"I'm afraid that is not going to be possible. This human is spoken for. She's already in a pact with me."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	227	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_0ae01579	"Oni"	"If that is so, why did she need a guide out?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	231	"Oni" "[what]"
lost_market_inside_f0bea80c	a	"I was merely busy for a moment, but am here now."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	234	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_b5715c22		Erin gapes at you, astonished.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	238	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_a306a950	e	"Wait... Aya?! You can... talk like that?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	242	e shocked "[what]"
lost_market_inside_53400403		Wait, she's not surprised that you're a fox... just surprised that you can talk?	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	244	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_677781ee	a	"Of course. I'm still me."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	246	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_aeccaa92		You address the oni.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	250	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_a4bbe595	a	"We must depart. Kindly find someone else to bargain with."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	253	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_40d4a211		The oni glares at you and crosses her arms.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	257	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_3a738350		The crowd around you becomes agitated.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	259	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_7950587b		You had better not linger.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	261	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_3e7b2561	a	"Erin, climb upon my back. I'll take us out of here."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	264	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_fe925a06	e	"Are you sure? Shouldn't we find that spell?"	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	266	e sad "[what]"
lost_market_inside_53976138		You shake your head.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	268	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_3c031729	a	"Not tonight."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	270	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_3f83c729		She reluctantly grabs hold of your fur and hauls herself onto your back, hugging your neck tightly.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	274	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_f63a96c6		You fly like the wind and take her back to the alley. The streets shift around you, but you know exactly where to go.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	279	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_f7eb623f	a	"Close your eyes."	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	281	a fox "[what]"
lost_market_inside_a16c14f8		You can't tell if she followed the instruction, so you just have to hope she heard you.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	283	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_6e803ed9		You race across the border between the spirit and mortal worlds. It's easier to leave with the both of you present.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	287	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_d1620709		The air around you blurs and you shift back, now holding Erin in your arms.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	290	"[what]"
lost_market_inside_34f55d1a		Her eyes are shut tight.	game/script files/8_lostmarket.rpy	292	"[what]"
